sec 7.4/8.5: in the second of its handing off the root's record anchors a fresh key's entry whose prev is the root's seq-3 twin; the record anchors what another key signed, so the root has not retired at it and it counts, while the twin, above the retiring seq, is made timely by no record of that second: RETIRED, no fork; the fresh key's entry EXCLUDED and the record's hash MISSING.
